    description: "OWNER DIRECTION 2026-08-23, recorded in their words: \"we should move forward\nwith INV-fibis/INV-nuhun under the assumption that we will add pyright etc in\ndue course.\"\n\nWHAT THIS IS. hypergumbo's declared architecture for receiver typing is\nmulti-fidelity analysis with coexistence (ADR-0012, spec section 20): where a\nreal language server is available, use its type resolution; fall through to\ntree-sitter when it is not; run BOTH rather than one replacing the other. That\nis already SHIPPED for Rust via rust-analyzer's SCIP output. Section 20 names\nthe next backends outright -- pyright, tsserver, gopls, JDT. This item is the\nPYTHON one.\n\nWHY PYTHON IS EASIER THAN THE RUST PRECEDENT, not harder: rust-analyzer\nEXECUTES build.rs, which is why that backend must stay opt-in and must never\nbe pointed at an untrusted repo. pyright performs pure static inference and\nexecutes nothing, so the safety argument that constrains the Rust backend does\nnot transfer. The dependency shape is the real cost: scip-python is an npm\npackage (@sourcegraph/scip-python), NOT on PyPI -- node and npm are present on\nthis box, but AGENTS.md's network allowlist names pip package installation and\ndoes not name npm, so CHECK ALLOWED_WEBSITES.md BEFORE assuming installability.\nThat check is a prerequisite, not a detail.\n\nWHAT IT WOULD CLOSE -- measured against the open set on 2026-08-23, not\nassumed:\n\n  LIKELY CLOSES\n  - INV-mumov (P2, python-only). Best candidate and nearly a direct hit: its\n    live gap is \"attribute-chain receivers carry no module hint (module slot\n    'external')\", i.e. obj.deep.method(), which is exactly what pyright knows.\n    CAUTION: that item's written STATEMENT is about whether an edge is emitted\n    at all, and its own title says that clause is already REFUTED, so re-read\n    the statement before closing rather than closing on the title.\n  - WI-sitos (P3, Django ORM) and WI-jojuv (P3, SQLAlchemy). Both are scoped\n    explicitly as \"I/O visibility via type-verified receiver typing\".\n    UNVERIFIED DEPENDENCY: pyright resolves these well only when the ANALYSED\n    repo has django-stubs / sqlalchemy stubs installed. That is a property of\n    the target repo's environment, not of hypergumbo, and must be measured\n    rather than assumed.\n\n  DENTS BUT DOES NOT CLOSE\n  - INV-linub (P2, the CLASS item). Its statement says \"for every language\";\n    python is 1 of 13. Kotlin and JavaScript fail an EARLIER link -- they emit\n    no call edge at all for an external instance-method call (WI-nasuf) -- so\n    there is no edge for any amount of type resolution to enrich.\n  - WI-makij (P2, chained method calls). Python's share improves; the item\n    spans more.\n\n  DOES NOT CLOSE, AND THIS IS THE POINT OF THE OWNER DIRECTION ABOVE\n  - INV-fibis (P0) and INV-nuhun (P1). Both are about the RESIDUAL: a clean\n    verdict must be honest about receivers it CANNOT type. pyright shrinks that\n    set and never empties it -- **kwargs, getattr, values out of json.loads, C\n    extensions without stubs, untyped third-party packages. Those two therefore\n    proceed on their own terms and are NOT BLOCKED on this item, which is why\n    no isbefore edge is filed in either direction.\n\nSECOND-ORDER BENEFIT, labelled as such rather than blurred into the above: this\nwould sharply cut disclosure VOLUME. Both figures are measured on hypergumbo's\nown tree at dev 30370c4cd6 -- 6,541 of 9,267 method call sites (70.6%) have an\nuntypeable receiver, and 63 of the 119 sites raised per host_fs claim are\n.replace(). Shrinking those makes the INV-fibis/INV-nuhun disclosures far more\nactionable while leaving both invariants exactly as open as they are now. That\nis improving the tool, not satisfying an invariant.\n\nTHE METRIC IS ALREADY BUILT. `unknown_receiver_scope` (shipped #481 boundary /\n#482 taint) reports untyped-receiver sites over method call sites. It cannot be\ngamed by adding catalogue rows -- only by genuinely typing more receivers -- so\nthat ratio IS this item's acceptance measure. Record the pre-number per repo\nbefore starting.\n\nSEQUENCING CAUTION: measurement 0001's <50% precision band sequences recall\nwork behind precision (WI-sivuz). This is recall work. It needs the marginal-\nprecision measurement that `0003` applied to the construction-edge widening\n(2.9% marginal precision) before it is believed to be a win."  # 6307
